1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,270
Microsoft's front door required
a VPN.

2
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:06,965
But its analytics API was still
reachable online.

3
00:00:07,215 --> 00:00:09,160
An AI agent found it

4
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:10,716
for a sixteen-year-old
researcher.

5
00:00:10,966 --> 00:00:13,059
For ten days, it worked through

6
00:00:13,059 --> 00:00:14,803
one security check after
another.

7
00:00:15,053 --> 00:00:17,168
The server checked the token's
claims,

8
00:00:17,168 --> 00:00:19,192
but never verified its
signature.

9
00:00:19,442 --> 00:00:22,070
Still, every email-style
username failed.

10
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:24,501
Then the researcher tried a
simpler name.

11
00:00:25,051 --> 00:00:25,714
Admin.

12
00:00:25,964 --> 00:00:28,223
This time, a test query returned
one.

13
00:00:28,473 --> 00:00:30,625
That meant seventeen databases,

14
00:00:30,625 --> 00:00:33,503
with an estimated seventeen
point three

15
00:00:33,503 --> 00:00:35,515
trillion rows potentially
reachable.

16
00:00:35,765 --> 00:00:38,886
He checked limited samples, then
reported the flaw.

17
00:00:39,136 --> 00:00:40,323
Microsoft restricted access

18
00:00:40,323 --> 00:00:43,596
and awarded him five thousand
dollars.

19
00:00:43,846 --> 00:00:45,686
So checking claims isn't enough.

20
00:00:45,936 --> 00:00:47,881
You have to verify the
signature.
